    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15784" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Engŭĭon</span></b>  (also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Engyon</span></b> ), i,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐγγύιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city</i> in the
			interior <i>of Sicily</i>, now <i>Gangi
				Vetere</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 14,
			249</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Engŭīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Enguion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, § 193</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Enguīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>its inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 5,
			72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8, 14, § 91</span></i>.</div>
